{"text": "From: \"Fuentes, Xiomara\" <xfuentes@fuenteslabor.example>\nTo: Hunter Abernathy-Lowe <hunter@sweetgrassbakery.example>\nCc: Leon Brathwaite <lbrathwaite@fuenteslabor.example>\nDate: Wed, 04 Mar 2026 16:52:10 -0600\nSubject: RE: Retainer + the Dang charge (EEOC No. 846-2026-01193)\n\nHunter,\n\nThanks -- received. Two housekeeping points before the substance:\n\n1. Please don't send card numbers by email again. I have deleted your message from our mail server, and Leon ran the card ending 4237 for the $3,500 retainer this afternoon (receipt no. R-118204). Next time use the payment page inside the portal.\n\n2. Change the portal password you mentioned today, and anywhere else you use it.\n\nNow the charge. The charging party, Dang Van Minh (you call him \"Minh\"; the EEOC paperwork has him as \"Mr. Dang\"), alleges national-origin discrimination and retaliation under Title VII. He says he was fired eleven days after he complained that your shift lead told him to \"speak English in my kitchen.\" He identifies as Vietnamese and says he is the only Asian employee on the morning shift. The timing is the problem, not the merits, and the comp claim makes the timing worse, not better. Do not talk to Brandi or anyone else on staff about why he was let go.\n\nOur position statement is due March 27, 2026. The investigator is Paula Okoye-Wright in the Dallas District Office, (972) 555-0181; all contact with her goes through me. See 29 C.F.R. § 1601.12 if you want to read what a charge has to contain.\n\nWhat I need from you by Monday:\n  - his complete personnel file, including the Form I-9 and any write-ups\n  - timecards and schedules, October through his last day\n  - the December no-show texts, as screenshots showing the date and his number\n  - names of everyone who was in the kitchen on January 5\n\nOn your last question (the dishwashers): call me, don't write. 214.555.0150 is my direct line.\n\nXiomara\n\nXiomara Fuentes | Fuentes Labor & Employment, PLLC\n500 N. Akard St., Ste. 1810, Dallas, TX 75201\nState Bar of Texas No. 24081177\nCONFIDENTIAL ATTORNEY-CLIENT COMMUNICATION. If you received this in error, delete it.\n\n> On Wed, Mar 4, 2026 at 11:07 AM Hunter Abernathy-Lowe <hunter@sweetgrassbakery.example> wrote:\n>\n> Xiomara - here's the card for the retainer. Visa 4429 4695 1655 4237 exp 08/28 cvv 614,\n> billing zip 75206. Name on the card is my husband's, Terrence Lowe.\n>\n> I logged into the portal like Leon said (user hunter.al, password Sweetgrass#2019 - I know,\n> I'll change it).\n>\n> Minh's last day was 1/16. He'd been with us since Aug 2021, most recently at $19.75/hr.\n> Honestly the timing looks bad, but he no-showed three times in December and I have the texts.\n> He also filed a comp claim for the oven burn on his forearm (claim # WC-TX-25-338104) back in\n> November, and Brandi thinks that's what this is really about.\n>\n> Also - is it a problem that I pay two of the dishwashers in cash? One of them doesn't have papers.\n>\n> Hunter\n> Sweetgrass Bakery & Cafe LLC, 2214 Greenville Ave, Dallas. 469-555-0125\n>\n>> On Tue, Mar 3, 2026 at 5:31 PM Xiomara Fuentes <xfuentes@fuenteslabor.example> wrote:\n>>\n>> Hunter, good talking today. The retainer is $3,500. Leon (my paralegal, cc'd) will set you up\n>> on the client portal: https://clients.fuenteslabor.example/login\n>> XF", "kind": "Email", "detail": "552 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Xiomara Fuentes", "Hunter Abernathy-Lowe", "Brandi", "Dang Van Minh", "Paula Okoye-Wright", "Xiomara", "Leon", "Minh", "Terrence Lowe"], "companies": ["Fuentes Labor & Employment", "Fuenteslabor", "Sweetgrass Bakery", "Dang", "Sweetgrass Bakery & Cafe LLC"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 1.300000000745058, "modelMs": 26535.800000000745, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "passport_dl", "routing", "phone", "record", "vin", "account", "money", "dob", "age90", "date", "street"